# rule|file|NaN|reason
# Used by scripts/style-check/style-check.ts. Keep the count exact: the check fails when it is too low as well.

# A Drop that runs while a panic unwinds must not panic: a second panic aborts the process.
poison|crates/habilis-network/src/transport/pool/in_flight_dial.rs|1|InFlightDial::drop clears the in-flight entry during unwinding. register_dial must read the same map.
poison|crates/habilis-network/src/transport/pool/unicast_pool.rs|1|register_dial reads the map that the in-flight drop clears: a poisoned lock is reached only from the pool

# The guard of a test must survive a test that panicked, or it hides the failure that matters.
poison|crates/habilis-network-test-tracing/src/guard.rs|2|lock helper of the test guard: the import and the call.

# The light-cycles example uses native generators, a nightly-only feature.
feature|crates/habilis-network-netplay/examples/light-cycles/native/game/src/lib.rs|1|coroutines, yield_expr (nightly example)
feature|crates/habilis-network-netplay/examples/light-cycles/native/visage-rust-tui/src/lib.rs|1|coroutines, coroutine_trait (nightly example)

# A panic must not cross the C boundary: this is the defence in depth that the guide allows.
catch_unwind|crates/habilis-network-ffi/src/ffi.rs|1|FFI boundary

# The one catch_unwind outside the FFI boundary: the helper that the tests use to check a panic.
catch_unwind|crates/habilis-network-test-tracing/src/guard.rs|1|catch_panic, the helper that the tests use to check a panic

# anyhow_pub: a public signature returns anyhow. Exceptions: test and benchmark helpers behind a
# feature, not library API.
anyhow_pub|crates/habilis-network-iroh-webrtc-transport/src/bench.rs|3|benchmark harness behind the bench feature, not library API

# glob: every glob import still to be replaced with explicit imports (tracker items G2 and G3). The rows go away with the fix.

# operator: an overload that has a math or logic meaning (U22). Each line names the meaning.

# pub_const_fn: a public const fn (U21). Each row is a count that may only go down.

# A hand-written Eq, Ord or PartialOrd: the compiler checks a derive, not a manual impl.

